	(layer "F.Cu")
	(descr "Cylindrical radial EDLC supercapacitor mounted HORIZONTALLY, MIRRORED orientation: the two radial leads (5.00 mm pitch) exit the end face and bend 90 deg down to the pads 2.5 mm in front of the face -- same simple bend as the original orientation, with the can extending the OTHER direction from the pads. Can axis parallel to the board, 10.0 mm tall lying on its side. Drawn for Eaton HV1020-2R7505-R (5.0 F, 2.7 V; ~40 mohm). Pad 1 = POSITIVE. *** DELIBERATELY NO COURTYARD OVER THE BODY *** - the can is glued down and may lie over other components, so the only keep-out is a small courtyard around the two legs, matching the house prismatic-horizontal convention. The body outline is on F.Fab as documentation only and generates no DRC. MECHANICAL: parts under the can must clear its underside (set by your standoff/glue line); parts under the 2.5 mm lead bend must stay low, since the lead descends there from the can's 5.0 mm mid-height to the board. Vertical alternative: stock Capacitor_THT:CP_Radial_D10.0mm_P5.00mm (20 mm standing). Datasheet: Eaton HV series cylindrical cells.")
	(tags "supercapacitor EDLC radial horizontal lay-down bent-lead glued no-keepout tht polarised HV1020")
